From bd2fed5b1d54164b63eac55d5da91859cb187b88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NXTORBIS TECHNOLOGIES <nxtorbis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:02:37 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Orbis: the address bar predicts again

Two things were stopping the list of predictions from appearing.

Orbis's own provider never told the omnibox it had finished when it had nothing to add -- Orbis not running, an answer
that would not parse, or simply no rows for what was typed. Chromium's controller then waits on it, and that wait is a
wait before anybody's rows appear: a working address bar made to look like a dead one by the one provider with nothing
to say. Every way out of Start and OnResponse now finishes properly.

And a line of debugging was left in the window message handler, opening, appending to and closing C:/chromium/embed-debug.log
on every window message that was not a mouse move. Two megabytes had collected. Inside the embedded browser that is the
whole stream of clicks, keys, focus changes and resizes, each one paying for a file write.
---
 components/omnibox/browser/orbis_provider.cc | 287 +++++++++++++++++++
 ui/views/win/hwnd_message_handler.cc         |   1 -
 2 files changed, 287 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 components/omnibox/browser/orbis_provider.cc

